Preserve rule guards and mapped runtime data

Branch and match continuations must match facts shared by their arms.
Dropping those facts derived conclusions without their guards and left
shared function results unbound during compilation.

Mapped tree operations must agree with the keys exposed by iteration.
Resolve mappings before structural edits and set operations, account for
filtered keys in lookups and lengths, and preserve copy-on-write
snapshots. Prune empty prefix restrictions so empty relations do not
appear nonempty.

Use an explicit isomorphism search stack because symmetric carriers can
require one search level per element and overflow the thread stack.

Cover these failures with integration regressions, seeded map
comparisons, and dynamic conversion checks with incremental state.
